    "report": {
      "assessment_status": "completed",
      "conclusion": "supported",
      "summary": "In the last 10 minutes of the authorized window (2026-10-16T04:46:27Z–04:56:27Z, policy-window-1), checkout's oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder span error ratio is 0.4737 (47.4%), not 100% and not zero: 20 spans carried STATUS_CODE_ERROR against 22.22 STATUS_CODE_UNSET in the same 600s increase, with a total PlaceOrder span rate of 0.0704 spans/s (~42 spans per 10 minutes). The only non-zero gRPC status among checkout's client RPCs is oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge with rpc_grpc_status_code=2 (~20 calls), while cart, currency, product-catalog, shipping and email calls all show status 0; payment's own server span grpc.oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge shows 20 STATUS_CODE_ERROR spans and its error ratio is 0.4865. The same ratio query over the preceding ~1h40m of a 2-hour view returned 0 at every step up to 04:41:27, with the first non-zero point at 04:46:27 (0.3636, then 0.923, then 0.4737), so the failure is recent and ongoing. A single sampled trace at 04:56:23 (trace f060d4ab0a282c88ecc47bb28b069858) shows a fully successful order — checkout PlaceOrder rpc.grpc.status_code=0, payment Charge rpc.grpc.status_code=0, frontend POST /api/checkout http.status_code=200 — confirming that this is a partial failure affecting a subset of orders, not a total outage. Because these are span counts (not unique requests) over low absolute volume, the ratio is indicative rather than a precise request failure rate, and the mechanism behind the Charge failures is not established by the evidence available in this Run."
    }
